{{also|suppe}}
==German==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|de|gml|suppe}}, {{m|gml|soppe}}, {{m|gml|sope}}, which spread under the reinforcing influence of {{der|de|fr|soupe}}. Both from {{der|de|gem-pro|*supô}}, {{m|gem-pro|*suppô}}, {{m|gem-pro|*suppǭ|t=broth, sop}}, which is related to {{cog|de|saufen||to drink}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈzʊpə/|aa=Germany}}
** {{audio|de|De-Suppe.ogg|aa=Germany}}
** {{audio|de|De-Suppe2.ogg|aa=Germany}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈsʊpɛ/|[ˈsupɛ]|aa=Austria,South German,Switzerland}}
** {{audio|de|De-at-Suppe.ogg|aa=Austria}}
* {{rhymes|de|ʊpə|s=2}}
* {{hyph|de|Sup|pe}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=^chen}}

# [[soup]]

====Usage notes====
* {{m|de|eine eingebrockte Suppe auslöffeln}} literally means to eat a breaded soup with the spoon and refers to an unhappy situation to pass.

